{"v":15,"id":"e13","kid":"emma","title":"The Dragon Boat Festival","zh":"端午节","level":"B1","genre":"节日文化","src":"facts","sum":"端午节在农历五月初五，相传与纪念屈原有关。赛龙舟、吃粽子是两大习俗，南北粽子口味不同。2009 年端午节入选联合国教科文组织非物质文化遗产名录。","words":308,"paras":[{"t":"The Dragon Boat Festival, also called Duanwu, takes place on the fifth day of the fifth month of the Chinese lunar calendar. It usually comes in late May or June, at the start of summer, and it has been celebrated for more than two thousand years.","w":[[0,3,"the",-1],[4,10,"dragon",0],[11,15,"boat",0],[16,24,"festival",0],[26,30,"also",-1],[31,37,"called",-1],[38,44,"Duanwu",-1],[46,51,"takes",1],[52,57,"place",1],[58,60,"on",-1],[61,64,"the",-1],[65,70,"fifth",-1],[71,74,"day",-1],[75,77,"of",-1],[78,81,"the",-1],[82,87,"fifth",-1],[88,93,"month",-1],[94,96,"of",-1],[97,100,"the",-1],[101,108,"chinese",-1],[109,114,"lunar",2],[115,123,"calendar",2],[125,127,"it",-1],[128,135,"usually",-1],[136,141,"comes",-1],[142,144,"in",-1],[145,149,"late",-1],[150,153,"May",-1],[154,156,"or",-1],[157,161,"june",-1],[163,165,"at",-1],[166,169,"the",-1],[170,175,"start",-1],[176,178,"of",-1],[179,185,"summer",-1],[187,190,"and",-1],[191,193,"it",-1],[194,197,"has",-1],[198,202,"been",-1],[203,213,"celebrated",-1],[214,217,"for",-1],[218,222,"more",-1],[223,227,"than",-1],[228,231,"two",-1],[232,240,"thousand",-1],[241,246,"years",-1]]},{"t":"The most popular story about the festival is about Qu Yuan, a poet and minister in the State of Chu long ago. Qu Yuan loved his country and gave the king wise advice, but other officials were jealous of him, and he was sent away. When he heard that his country had been defeated, he was so sad that he jumped into the Miluo River. The local people loved him. They rowed their boats out quickly to look for him and beat drums to scare the fish away. They also threw rice into the river so that the fish would eat the rice instead.","w":[[0,3,"the",-1],[4,8,"most",-1],[9,16,"popular",-1],[17,22,"story",-1],[23,28,"about",-1],[29,32,"the",-1],[33,41,"festival",-1],[42,44,"is",-1],[45,50,"about",-1],[51,53,"Qu",3],[54,58,"Yuan",3],[60,61,"a",-1],[62,66,"poet",-1],[67,70,"and",-1],[71,79,"minister",-1],[80,82,"in",-1],[83,86,"the",-1],[87,92,"State",4],[93,95,"of",4],[96,99,"Chu",4],[100,104,"long",-1],[105,108,"ago",-1],[110,112,"Qu",3],[113,117,"Yuan",3],[118,123,"loved",-1],[124,127,"his",-1],[128,135,"country",-1],[136,139,"and",-1],[140,144,"gave",-1],[145,148,"the",-1],[149,153,"king",-1],[154,158,"wise",-1],[159,165,"advice",-1],[167,170,"but",-1],[171,176,"other",-1],[177,186,"officials",-1],[187,191,"were",-1],[192,199,"jealous",5],[200,202,"of",5],[203,206,"him",-1],[208,211,"and",-1],[212,214,"he",-1],[215,218,"was",-1],[219,223,"sent",6],[224,228,"away",6],[230,234,"when",-1],[235,237,"he",-1],[238,243,"heard",-1],[244,248,"that",-1],[249,252,"his",-1],[253,260,"country",-1],[261,264,"had",-1],[265,269,"been",-1],[270,278,"defeated",-1],[280,282,"he",-1],[283,286,"was",-1],[287,289,"so",-1],[290,293,"sad",-1],[294,298,"that",-1],[299,301,"he",-1],[302,308,"jumped",-1],[309,313,"into",-1],[314,317,"the",-1],[318,323,"Miluo",7],[324,329,"river",7],[331,334,"the",-1],[335,340,"local",-1],[341,347,"people",-1],[348,353,"loved",-1],[354,357,"him",-1],[359,363,"they",-1],[364,369,"rowed",-1],[370,375,"their",-1],[376,381,"boats",-1],[382,385,"out",-1],[386,393,"quickly",-1],[394,396,"to",-1],[397,401,"look",8],[402,405,"for",8],[406,409,"him",-1],[410,413,"and",-1],[414,418,"beat",-1],[419,424,"drums",-1],[425,427,"to",-1],[428,433,"scare",9],[434,437,"the",9],[438,442,"fish",9],[443,447,"away",9],[449,453,"they",-1],[454,458,"also",-1],[459,464,"threw",-1],[465,469,"rice",-1],[470,474,"into",-1],[475,478,"the",-1],[479,484,"river",-1],[485,487,"so",10],[488,492,"that",10],[493,496,"the",-1],[497,501,"fish#2",-1],[502,507,"would",-1],[508,511,"eat",-1],[512,515,"the",-1],[516,520,"rice",-1],[521,528,"instead",-1]]},{"t":"Two customs come from this story. The first is dragon boat racing. A dragon boat is long and narrow, with a dragon's head at the front and a tail at the back. A team of about twenty paddlers sits in pairs, and a drummer at the front keeps the rhythm. The team must paddle together perfectly to win. Dragon boat racing is now popular around the world, from Canada to Australia.","w":[[0,3,"two",-1],[4,11,"customs",-1],[12,16,"come",-1],[17,21,"from",-1],[22,26,"this",-1],[27,32,"story",-1],[34,37,"the",-1],[38,43,"first",-1],[44,46,"is",-1],[47,53,"dragon",11],[54,58,"boat",11],[59,65,"racing",11],[67,68,"a",-1],[69,75,"dragon",-1],[76,80,"boat",-1],[81,83,"is",-1],[84,88,"long",-1],[89,92,"and",-1],[93,99,"narrow",-1],[101,105,"with",-1],[106,107,"a",-1],[108,116,"dragon's",-1],[117,121,"head",-1],[122,124,"at",-1],[125,128,"the",-1],[129,134,"front",-1],[135,138,"and",-1],[139,140,"a",-1],[141,145,"tail",-1],[146,148,"at",-1],[149,152,"the",-1],[153,157,"back",-1],[159,160,"a",-1],[161,165,"team",-1],[166,168,"of",-1],[169,174,"about",-1],[175,181,"twenty",-1],[182,190,"paddlers",-1],[191,195,"sits",-1],[196,198,"in",12],[199,204,"pairs",12],[206,209,"and",-1],[210,211,"a",-1],[212,219,"drummer",-1],[220,222,"at",-1],[223,226,"the",-1],[227,232,"front",-1],[233,238,"keeps",13],[239,242,"the",13],[243,249,"rhythm",13],[251,254,"the",-1],[255,259,"team",-1],[260,264,"must",-1],[265,271,"paddle",-1],[272,280,"together",-1],[281,290,"perfectly",-1],[291,293,"to",-1],[294,297,"win",-1],[299,305,"dragon",11],[306,310,"boat",11],[311,317,"racing",11],[318,320,"is",-1],[321,324,"now",-1],[325,332,"popular",-1],[333,339,"around",-1],[340,343,"the",-1],[344,349,"world",-1],[351,355,"from",-1],[356,362,"canada",-1],[363,365,"to",-1],[366,375,"australia",-1]]},{"t":"The second custom is eating zongzi. These are made of sticky rice wrapped in bamboo or reed leaves and tied with string. In northern China, many people like sweet zongzi with red dates or bean paste. In the south, many people prefer salty ones with pork or egg yolk.","w":[[0,3,"t